  <result aggregation-status="1" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Rights in Africa Report</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The report focused on 24 countries focusing on Internet Freedom (with sub-themes including Internet access and disruptions; Free speech and Media freedoms; and Privacy and Surveillance); Data Governance (policies, laws and Digital IDs); Review of the Universal Service Fund; and Developments in ICT and Emerging Technologies (some of which include Artificial Intelligence Strategies, inclusion of ICTs in National Action Plans or Strategies). 

The report has informed the interventions and advocacy we have staged in various countries where we are present and the report also took centre stage at one of the sessions of the African Internet Governance Forum held in Abuja on the 21st of September 2023, where we received immense contribution and feedback. One of such feedback was seeing increased interest in the use of the Universal Service Fund. During this session, we witnessed a few government organisations desire to learn how to utilise it better while other stakeholders required more accountability from them.</narrative>
   </description>
